{"title":"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(less_trig_required,_use_of_quadratic_formula)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (less trig required, use of quadratic formula)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/f/3bf6435cdb21ba250983f7564431857eaf042741.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x+\\tan y=25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"142\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/a/4da25d192ad56696005fd2f796c4c260c6be3e72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot x + \\cot y=30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"138\" height=\"16\" />, what is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/8/0b8fe4677d593d12394afac5a6d1e1d4e9c29cf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f7a6780175ccfa1b4a7a1a093a37a39358498f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot$\" width=\"23\" height=\"11\" /> is the reciprocal function of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/b/75b04387daddfdad2ef55b5a9dfec552ea41db50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan$\" width=\"26\" height=\"11\" />:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/5/045d6ed7947d981c6658b8b0162d5d42dc57c6c7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cot x + \\cot y = \\frac{1}{\\tan x} + \\frac{1}{\\tan y} = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan y}{\\tan x \\cdot \\tan y} = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"400\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/6/a66609a5380e81f22c1b260eed90ee21a072405c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x \\cdot \\tan y = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan y}{30} = \\frac{25}{30} = \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"306\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>Using the tangent addition formula: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/b/39b9673fa2566f9fb3794b1fa5c54325ba12c853.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x+y) = \\frac{\\tan x + \\tan y}{1-\\tan x \\cdot \\tan y} = \\frac{25}{1-\\frac{5}{6}} = \\boxed{150}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"367\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the formula for tangent of a sum, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/b/f2b4dedb62b9910c00b89f7ad03fa0865e391002.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x+y)=\\frac{\\tan x + \\tan y}{1-\\tan x \\tan y} = \\frac{25}{1-\\tan x \\tan y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"363\" height=\"41\" />. We only need to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/f/a5f0eab1707ac95208ec8d04450218b9dc40c014.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan x \\tan y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"83\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c1f89d47dac13556ac6e519dcef80304da6f96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25 = \\tan x + \\tan y = \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} + \\frac{\\sin y}{\\cos y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"270\" height=\"40\" />. Cross multiplying, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c4700f7923b4c8e7471c96d2aa14588580b5b93c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{\\sin x \\cos y + \\cos x \\sin y}{\\cos x \\cos y} = \\frac{\\sin(x+y)}{\\cos x \\cos y} = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"326\" height=\"42\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a43ce158c87a47b3880f6099713ff3cca5e14c3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30 = \\cot x + \\cot y = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} + \\frac{\\cos y}{\\sin y} = \\frac{\\cos x \\sin y + \\sin x \\cos y}{\\sin x \\sin y} = \\frac{\\sin(x+y)}{\\sin x \\sin y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"579\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p><p>Dividing:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/4/e4493364ad0b730ee0b909762a491e0555dc76f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{30} = \\frac{\\frac{\\sin(x+y)}{\\cos x \\cos y}}{\\frac{\\sin(x+y)}{\\sin x \\sin y}} = \\frac{\\sin x \\sin y}{\\cos x \\cos y} = \\tan x \\tan y = \\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"359\" height=\"56\" />. Plugging in to the earlier formula, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/1/4d1c81f206d4160fc818be9a167b649d93d9f159.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x+y) = \\frac{25}{1-\\frac{5}{6}} = \\frac{25}{\\frac{1}{6}} = \\boxed{150}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"262\" height=\"44\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28less_trig_required.2C_use_of_quadratic_formula.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(less_trig_required,_use_of_quadratic_formula)\">Solution 3 (less trig required, use of quadratic formula)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (less trig required, use of quadratic formula)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/5/5853e00a37342137b8d7e44a225d162c3aa7f7f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=\\tan x$\" width=\"73\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/9/1b92e3212dd9a91dfa6e3dad2d086a1b442497ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=\\tan y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"16\" />. This simplifies the equations to:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/1/281c4cc8f2ed8a01aac5bb59e1bde48213be807d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a + b = 25\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/a/6fa5ecaffcb1fdd63999239646bdd9c3e4ce7c86.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{b} = 30\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Taking the tangent of a sum formula from Solution 2, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c76e41a2835558ceba96036a7f638a72a240c903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tan(x+y) = \\frac{25}{1 - ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"161\" height=\"40\" />. \n</p><p>We can use substitution to solve the system of equations from above: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/d/f3d27b61293e09d91f4d4cbb7c1a66cd90ed6e38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = -a + 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/a/61a2e83b792ea48d5efe89c2c1e757ef49c81496.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a} + \\frac{1}{-a + 25} = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"145\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p>Multiplying by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/5/4c5ff82d5010c91fa94dbd2e23028ea174e54825.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-a(a-25)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"18\" />,  we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/4/7b42f46931e8f9ee83593852cc5399db26a8c804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + (-a + 25) = -30a(a-25)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"18\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/4998d101fba359ef99a8404ce7d815f4dd3a2e8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-30a^2 + 750a = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"150\" height=\"16\" />. Dividing everything by 5 and shifting everything to one side gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a35b8773b7d4b1c1fb51920d5acff8e16f9f2057.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6a^2 - 150a + 5 = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Using the quadratic formula gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/c/82ca1e62e5a5d5ef1fa294ddc14647e29421a663.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{150 \\pm \\sqrt {22380}}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"146\" height=\"41\" />. Since this looks too hard to simplify, we can solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/d/b0dd2ebd4491bc6479d0745f529e4062c6d883ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b = 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"14\" />, which turns out to also be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a8412a6db7de9593eadc64c1f671e8e44e6aa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{150 \\pm \\sqrt {22380}}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"41\" />, provided that the sign of the radical in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is opposite the one in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>WLOG, assume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/9/ea988c4f6e3a2f88dce82ec06ae2f26a8e74d824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\frac{150 + \\sqrt{22380}}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"146\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ecd27112d04df20e37211a1e3b30ec106bd2027.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{150 - \\sqrt{22380}}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"144\" height=\"41\" />. Multiplying them gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/7/b17c8fa738e53597edf6e5cf7d4680015f97034a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab = \\frac{22500 - 22380}{144}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"38\" /> which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/3/5533bc48602603f16d18c04858cad119c04833c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>THe denominator of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/7400c78bb908489403da4d3b5efa71a258909107.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{25}{1 - ab}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"51\" height=\"38\" /> ends up being <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/b/43ba19be0e30b99142416ebfbe17670437c8453e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, so multiplying both numerator and denominator by 6 gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/4649b1f9c320291995474a6d45af1bf004dc433f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{150}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-ThisUsernameIsTaken\n</p><p><br />\n</p><p>Remark: The quadratic need not be solved. The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/8/ef870ce9fefe09b80a97b05a7b9198414c1b35f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> can be found through Vieta's.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME\" title=\"1986 AIME\">1986 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1986 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1986 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\">AIME Problems and Solutions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=American_Invitational_Mathematics_Examination\" title=\"American Invitational Mathematics Examination\">American Invitational Mathematics Examination</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mathematics_competition_resources\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Mathematics competition resources\">Mathematics competition resources</a></li></ul>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017155529\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.059 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 279/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 8118/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.984      1 -total\n 61.22%    7.949      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.04%    4.809      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2815:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017155529 and revision id 199587. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}